# Settings for the first boot of your EmuStation.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy it to "emulationstation.txt" in the same folder (this boot partition).
#   2. Remove the "#" at the start of the lines you want, and change the values.
#   3. Put the card (or disk) back and boot. The file is read at EVERY boot.
#
# After it was used, the file is renamed to "emulationstation.txt.applied".
# In that copy, every password is replaced by "***". Lines that could not be
# used are listed at the end of the copy, with the reason.
#
# Rules:
#   - One setting per line: KEY=VALUE. Write the value as it is. Do not use $ or escapes.
#   - Spaces in a value are kept. A pair of quotes around the whole value ("..." or '...')
#     is removed. Use quotes if your value starts or ends with a space.
#   - A value must not contain control characters. Such a line is ignored.
#   - Unknown keys are ignored.
#   - The file on this partition can be read by anyone who holds the card. Passwords
#     are masked in the .applied copy, but they are visible in this file until the boot.

# Host name of the device. Letters a-z (lower case), digits and "-", up to 63 characters.
# Note: the HTTPS certificate is only valid for the host names it was built with
# (HOSTNAME and TLS_EXTRA_SANS in build.conf). If you use another name,
# the browser shows a certificate warning. The boot log says so.
#HOSTNAME=emulationstation

# Wi-Fi. Both lines are needed (on the Raspberry Pi also WIFI_COUNTRY, see below). The password has 8 to 63 characters (or 64 hex digits).
# "WIFI_SSID=" with an empty value removes the Wi-Fi setting made by this file.
# If the line is not in the file, the Wi-Fi setting stays as it is.
#WIFI_SSID=MyNetwork
#WIFI_PASSWORD=my wifi password

# Wi-Fi country, two capital letters (for example DE, US, GB). Raspberry Pi only.
# It sets the Wi-Fi channels of your country. Without it, Wi-Fi uses fewer, safe channels.
# Set it together with the Wi-Fi lines above. If it is missing, the country from the
# build (WIFI_COUNTRY in build.conf) is used.
#WIFI_COUNTRY=DE

# Time zone, as a name from the tz database.
#TIMEZONE=Europe/Berlin

# Keyboard layout, for example de, us, gb, fr.
#KEYMAP=de

# New password for the Linux user "emulationstation" (SSH and console login).
#USER_PASSWORD=change me

# New login for the web page. You can set only the user, only the password, or both.
#WEB_USER=zocken
#WEB_PASSWORD=change me too
